        <referenceFunction amount="1" category="transport systems" datasetRelatesToProduct="true" generalComment="A standard hybrid overpass was considered, which crosses 2 railway tracks. The overpass measures 6 m wide and 49 m long. On both sides there is a staircase (2.75 m x 20 m) and two ramps (2.75 m x 37 m) that end on a plateau (6 m x 5 m). In total (including stairs, ramps and plateau), the area of such an overpasse is 642m2. For larger (over three or more tracks) overpasses, it is assumed that the materialisation per m2 is similar, as it usually also requires an additional ramp and stairs. The data for the material requirements comes from SBB (pers. comm. SBB, 2019). Offcuts and rejects are not taken into account. It is assumed that the excavated material will be used elsewhere and not deposited. The energy requirement for the construction work (excluding excavation) was derived from an SBB LCA study on the construction of a platform per tonne of material installed (Rüegsegger &amp; Schori, 2017). The ecoinvent standard values were used for transport distances for material deliveries by lorry (Frischknecht et al., 2007).&#10;&#10;According to SBB, the service life of such an overpass is 78 years (pers. comm., SBB, 2024). Maintenance work, refurbishment and dismantling of the overpass are not taken into account.; UUID:e66e9555-cf47-33e9-9ed4-1a7d343c84bc" includedProcesses="The inventory includes all the materials, energy and transport necessary for constructing a pedestrian overpass over 2 railway tracks. Excluded are maintenance and disposal" infrastructureIncluded="true" infrastructureProcess="false" localCategory="transport systems" localName="Pedestrian overpass, over 2 tracks" localSubCategory="train\operations\infrastructure" name="Pedestrian overpass, over 2 tracks" subCategory="train\operations\infrastructure" unit="m2a">
